cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use do-math, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "do-math"
abstract: "do-math is a system for autonomous mathematical research in which many AI sessions, each a separate conversation, work on one mathematical statement. Every result the research keeps is a declaration in one Lean 4 library with a written record beside it. Each addition that comes out of a session's research is produced by one session, turned into a change to the library by a second session and judged by a third, and it is published with that judgment. A run is complete only when the Lean statement fixed at the start, or its negation, is settled through a proof that is complete in Lean and depends only on the allowed axioms."
authors:
  - family-names: "Kim"
    given-names: "Jaehyoung"
    affiliation: "Kyungpook National University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MegasKomnenos/do-math"
url: "https://github.com/MegasKomnenos/do-math"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - "autonomous mathematical research"
  - "multi-agent system"
  - "large language models"
  - "Lean 4"
